      "content": "To address inconsistent color transfer, start by checking the heat press's temperature profiles. Ensure the temperature range is within the recommended specifications for your fabric type (3.2-4.0 for polyester). Also, verify the pressure settings, as excessive pressure can damage the fabric or affect transfer. Additionally, check the substrate's temperature, as it may not be reaching the recommended 350-400°F for optimal transfer. Double-check your heat press's calibration to ensure it's functioning correctly.",
