      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The irregular patches and random fading could be related to the humidity environment around the heat press. High humidity can cause uneven ink solubility and accelerated degradation, leading to these issues. Check the humidity levels around the press, as a range of 30-50% relative humidity is usually optimal for sublimation printing. Additionally, inspect the ink itself for any visible signs of degradation, fading, or pigment settling, which could also contribute to the issues.",
